course: dictionary
lesson: 15128
title: Good enough and acceptable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Satisfactorily is an adverb, so it tells you how something was done. It comes from the word satisfy, which means to please or to meet what is needed. When a job is done satisfactorily, it has met what was needed.
explain: «Mia completed her project satisfactorily.» This means her project was done well enough to be accepted. It does not have to be perfect. Ask yourself: was the job good enough? If yes, satisfactorily fits.
explain: In school reports, «working satisfactorily» means a pupil is doing well enough. It is not the top praise, which would be excellent. In maths, «the problem was solved satisfactorily» means the answer was checked and met the rule of the sum.
fact: Satisfactorily means in a way that is good enough or acceptable.
fact: Satisfactorily can also mean in a way that meets a rule or a need.
fact: «Satisfactory» is the adjective, as in «a satisfactory answer».
fact: «Completed satisfactorily» means finished well enough to be accepted.
fact: Satisfactorily sounds more formal than saying «well enough», so you will often see it in reports and letters.
exercise: «Tom finished his homework satisfactorily.» What does satisfactorily mean here? | Without any help at all | Very quickly and loudly | In a way that is perfect and amazing | *In a way that is good enough
exercise: «The teacher said Ruby is progressing satisfactorily.» What does this tell you? | She is the best in the class | She has stopped learning | She is late every day | *She is improving well enough
exercise: Find and copy the adverb in this sentence: «The plant grew satisfactorily in the sunny window.» | *satisfactorily | sunny | window | plant
test: «Ben answered the maths question satisfactorily after he checked his working.» Why does this mean his answer was acceptable? | Because he wrote it in red pen | Because he wrote it very slowly | Because it was the only answer on the page | *Because it met the rule of the sum and was checked
test: A school report says «working satisfactorily». What does this mean? | Doing the best in the whole school | Doing nothing at all | *Doing well enough, though not excellent | Doing the work late
exam: «The broken gate was repaired satisfactorily, so the class could use the playground again.» What does satisfactorily mean? | Very quickly and noisily | Without any tools at all | In a way that nobody noticed | *In a way that is good enough and acceptable
